{
  "text": " I didn't, he began, and stopped, because Ask was looking at him over his spectacles with no expression whatever. At the spur, he said, yesterday, the boards, when they carried him up the bank. I took the head of the boards at the lip for the last two paces. They'd have had to set him down on the stones otherwise, he swallowed. I knew I shouldn't. I knew it while I was doing it. I'd like it known that I'd do it again.",
